      "math_academy_id": "e-5562",
      "problem": "Find $H^{\\perp}$ if ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14275210/assets/cb4658b87576adb05a3d3c05a32330ba86c9817c81accfe5fd3573ab2dccef45.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "Let's denote the vectors that span the subspace $H$ as $\\mathbf{h}_1$ and $\\mathbf{h}_2.$ \n\nA vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14275210/assets/7b486d1790a7fa70f4b558fc92dfddf2ace842c1f14f9bf060240afd071d517e.svg) belongs to $H^{\\perp}$ if $\\mathbf{x}\\cdot \\mathbf{h}_1=0$ and $\\mathbf{x}\\cdot \\mathbf{h}_2=0.$ So, we need to solve the following system:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14275210/assets/b4f5ea7a7ba57ec5f9946c1ba5f993c7b4884a69668f372859ac4502a8bf066b.svg) \n\nWe write the corresponding augmented matrix $M$ and reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, we have $2$ pivot columns (the $1$st and the $2$nd ones), so $x_3$ is a free variable. From the second equation we get $x_2=-\\dfrac{1}{3}x_3.$ Substituting this into first equation, we obtain $x_1 = -\\dfrac{1}{3}x_3.$\n\nSo, the general solution to the system is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14275210/assets/5b616909529c7aced6186e262672016aa3fb51a71a6a083ad8bd69e1d15f51bf.svg)\n\nTherefore, our orthogonal complement is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14275210/assets/19834aea3eb4e668e43df31bf6dcc014d366accaeb0eaf218ff0e5381cf5109a.svg)",
